      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's just subjective bias. we're just biological machines with chemical impulses. if the logic is that the net impact is zero, then the \"choice\" to suffer is just an irrational attachment to a temporary state. if i look at it purely logically, exiting the system isn't a tragedy, it's just a way to balance the equation. wouldn't you agree that from a purely objective standpoint, there's no logical reason to favor existence over non-existence?",
